descriptions.job-1tbaqsx:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio lays the foundations that help Stripe accelerate. We do this by creating, evolving, and maintaining Stripe&#39;s high-quality, versatile, and forward-looking brand design systems, experiences, and advertising campaigns. We sweat the details. We make it seem effortless. The Experiential team is responsible for bringing Stripe&#39;s brand to life in the real world, from flagship events and industry conferences to internal summits and curated partner experiences. This team operates at the intersection of creativity, strategy, technology, and production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Brand Designers at Stripe demonstrate a passion for the craft of design and a deep understanding of how design communicates brand essence. You will be responsible for defining and advancing Stripe&#39;s experiential design systems across physical experiences, digital surfaces, and mainstage creative content. You work at the intersection of design systems, concepting, and storytelling, creating design frameworks that scale while still feeling intentional and human. The ideal candidate is technically fluent, conceptually strong, crisply articulates design decisions, and collaborates seamlessly with creative directors, producers, marketers, communications, and engineering partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the end-to-end design of experiential programs, from early concepts and storytelling through detailed design, production, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Stripe’s brand and product strategy into compelling physical, digital, and hybrid experiences for global audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable visual identities, design systems, and toolkits for events and environments that extend Stripe’s evolving brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with producers, marketers, product teams, and senior stakeholders to define goals, make tradeoffs, and deliver work on time and at a high bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Art direct agencies, fabricators, contractors, and other external partners; provide clear feedback and uphold quality through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design keynote and presentation systems that make complex ideas feel clear, cohesive, and engaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve the Experiential Design discipline by sharing craft knowledge, improving team practices, and mentoring other designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experiential, environmental, brand, or integrated design experience, ideally for technology or product-led companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in art, design, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating concept-to-production work across events, environments, installations, keynotes, or other immersive brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large-scale conferences, trade shows, executive or customer events, or comparable IRL and hybrid experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual design, art direction, and storytelling skills across physical and digital media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently lead complex work while influencing designers, agencies, contractors, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment in incorporating stakeholder feedback while protecting the core creative idea and quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with motion design systems and how to apply them consistently across contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of design principles: layout, grid systems, typography, color, iconography, and photo art direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to designing for live event environments: LED walls, stage visuals, real-time rendering, and large-format displays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with design collaboration tools, including Figma and Keynote, and a systems-thinking approach to extending design systems across shared patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of emerging AI tools and how they fit into a professional creative production workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record delivering high quality work independently, and in close collaboration with cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find a meaningful balance between optimizing for speed, quality, and doing challenging, interesting, frame-perfect work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions and crave feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and have them help you learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, with a drive for perfection down to the last pixel or inch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about Stripe&#39;s mission, are dedicated to a user-first mindset, and have experience working with data and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience designing within real-world production constraints, including materials, fabrication, installation, wayfinding, accessibility, and on-site iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable experiential identity systems across multiple locations, audiences, or event formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort experimenting with emerging technologies where they improve storytelling or audience participation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, low-ego approach to critique, mentoring, and learning across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

descriptions.job-1i9flv5:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe, LLC. is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Tax team stakeholders to design and implement features of our financial systems that include Oracle Cloud Applications (Financials, TRCS, Fusion Tax), Stripe homegrown Tax Solutions and many other tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to automate Tax processes, work on transformation initiatives, implement SOX controls and maintain our financial Applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Finance systems (primarily Tax area including but not limited to Direct and Indirect Taxes) projects and strategic initiatives - including implementation of new tools and business process changes - from requirements, tool selection, system design, implementation, UAT, training, go-live &amp;amp; post go-live support.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technology liaison with Tax stakeholders to understand their pain points, opportunities for process improvements, automation &amp;amp; efficiency gains, create strategic roadmap and provide them with technology solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate an understanding of increasingly complex sales tax, transfer pricing and Tax provisioning concepts and effectively apply knowledge to develop and maintain tax systems and data flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design solutions and make architecture decisions by benchmarking with industry best practices to help us scale for the future.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering product teams to develop &amp;amp; deliver technical solutions to optimize financial workflow and integration with other Stripe internal systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and maintain the Fusion Tax and Integrate with homegrown Tax system for Indirect Tax determination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Tax Applications Configure &amp;amp; Maintain Systems Data protection &amp;amp; integrity Tax Compliance &amp;amp; SOX controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must have a Bachelor&#39;s degree or foreign equivalent in Engineering, Computer Science, Finance or a related field, plus 8 years of experience in Building and maintaining tax systems, of which, at least 5 years must be post-bachelors progressive experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Must also have 8 years of experience in each of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and implementing finance and compliance products at global scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tax systems including Sabrix, Vertex, Oracle EBTax and Fusion Cloud Tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program or project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing Internal Financial systems for Indirect or Direct Tax needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting development using SQL, PL/SQL, or BI Publisher.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taxation methods including VAT, Sales Tax, or GST, and related global compliance and reporting needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary: $274,456.00 - $334,600.00/yr.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This salary range represents the base salary range for the role and any sales commissions/sales bonuses targets, if applicable, would be in addition to the base salary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;40 hrs/week&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;50% Telecommuting permitted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Multiple Positions Available.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additional benefits for this role may include: equity, company bonus or sales commissions/bonuses; 401(k) plan; medical, dental, and vision benefits; and wellness stipends. &lt;strong&gt;CA36&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-DNI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;

descriptions.job-0m36641:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ready to do the most impactful work of your career? At&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/?utm_campaign=mt_o_m_w_m_m__coi_0_jd-onchain&amp;amp;utm_source=coinbase&quot;&gt;Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;, we are uncompromising on our mission to increase economic freedom. The bar is high, the environment is intense, and we like it that way. This isn&#39;t a place for complacency, it’s a place to be pushed past your perceived limits. If you&#39;re ready to build the future of finance alongside people who refuse to settle for &quot;good enough,&quot; you belong here. Coinbase is a remote-first, but not remote-only company. Expect to get together quarterly for intense in-person working sessions called “surges.”&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coinbase.com/careers&quot;&gt;learn more about working at Coinbase&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Credit Risk Analyst to join the Counterparty and Credit Risk team within Financial &amp;amp; Operational Risk. This team manages credit exposure across Coinbase&#39;s global institutional client base, underwriting counterparties and delivering lending solutions in a fast-evolving digital asset market. You&#39;ll own credit analysis for complex counterparties, recommend risk-based limits, and monitor portfolio exposures that directly inform how Coinbase scales its institutional products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own diligence and underwriting of institutional counterparties including hedge funds, asset managers, private equity, and venture capital firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recommend internal credit ratings and risk-based limits, preparing written analysis that substantiates each assessment for senior leadership review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor portfolio exposures, conduct periodic surveillance of trading partners, and clearly communicate concentration trends and settlement risks to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze asset volatility and liquidity risks on a per-asset and portfolio basis to inform limit-setting and capital planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate industry documentation (e.g., PBAs, MLAs, and ACAs) and collaborate with business development, operations, legal, and product teams to resolve complex client or product challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3 years of hands-on credit risk management experience, including counterparty underwriting or portfolio monitoring in a fast-moving financial services or digital asset environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience covering institutional clients such as hedge funds, asset managers, private equity, or venture capital firms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of capital markets products and standard industry documentation (PBAs, MLAs, prime brokerage agreements).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to produce clear written credit memos and present risk recommendations to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency building quantitative credit models and exposure analyses using spreadsheets, SQL, or other analytical tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilizes generative AI responsibly, maintaining human oversight to deliver business-ready outputs and drive measurable improvements in workflow efficiency, cost, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;P77678&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Transparency Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Base salary varies by location (see range below). Total compensation may also include equity and bonus eligibility, and benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k)).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual base salary range (excluding equity and bonus):&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$95,030&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$111,800 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic; font-size: 8pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Application Limit: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Candidates may submit a maximum of 3 applications within a 6-month period.&lt;/li&gt;
